<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.77 million bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.77 million bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's state-run Cotton Export Corporation (CEC) said on Friday 1996/97 (July-June) cotton output had reached a provisional 8.77 million 375-lb bales by June 12, down from 9.95 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Delivery and ginning figures in million bales (year-ago):</p>
<p>		    Punjab	   Sindh	    Total</p>
<p> Delivery	 6.690 (8.179)  2.084 (1.771)  8.774 (9.951)</p>
<p> Pressed	  6.690 (8.179)  2.084 (1.771)  8.774 (9.951)</p>
<p> Mill sales     6.295 (7.055)  2.016 (1.283)  8.312 (8.338)</p>
<p> Export sales   0.008 (1.023)  0.018 (0.481)  0.027 (1.505)</p>
<p> CEC		nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)</p>
<p> Unsold	   0.386 (0.100)  0.049 (0.006)  0.435 (0.106)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
